SOAPBOX: First time participating in the French REF DX Contest in the QRP 
SOAPBOX: category, and overall a very enjoyable experience. I operated 
SOAPBOX: with an FT-897D at 5 W output, antenna is LW 6m Up. Propagation 
SOAPBOX: was quite variable, but during certain periods the skip worked 
SOAPBOX: surprisingly well. 

80 m was challenging and required lot of 
SOAPBOX: patience, but I still managed to log a decent number of stations. 
SOAPBOX: The best results came in the morning on 7 MHz and in the 
SOAPBOX: afternoon on 14 MHz. Unfortunately, the skip on 21 and 28 MHz was 
SOAPBOX: closed towards France throughout the contest.

Very satisfied 
SOAPBOX: with the outcome, especially considering QRP and the current 
SOAPBOX: antenna setup. Looking forward to the next contest?hopefully with 
SOAPBOX: an improved antenna. See you on the bands!
